WEBVTT

00:12.060 --> 00:13.979
When I saw her pretending to play dumb

00:14.730 --> 00:16.064
I knew that was my chance.

00:17.190 --> 00:19.067
At that point, I kinda figured…

00:19.151 --> 00:20.736
"Amamiya probably likes her."

00:21.445 --> 00:22.988
And I'm sure it's mutual.

00:23.989 --> 00:24.865
I could tell.

00:25.866 --> 00:28.994
But I could also tell she was never
gonna make the first move.

00:29.536 --> 00:31.121
She'll make all sorts of excuses,

00:31.204 --> 00:32.831
keep pretending not to notice

00:33.749 --> 00:37.627
And pathetically do whatever it takes
to protect herself from getting hurt.

00:38.628 --> 00:41.506
She's a weakling who gets her
validation and happiness from

00:41.590 --> 00:43.467
others instead of herself.

00:44.051 --> 00:46.053
A passive girl who just sits and waits.

00:47.929 --> 00:49.222
Ugh.

00:49.806 --> 00:51.141
I really hate her.

00:52.684 --> 00:56.980
EPISODE 15
CLOUDS AND RAIN

00:58.148 --> 01:00.650
The Meiten band's gonna be
putting on a concert soon.

01:00.734 --> 01:02.944
Did you hear Akahoshi talking about it?

01:03.028 --> 01:03.945
Oh…

01:04.446 --> 01:07.032
You know what, I think the
guys did say something.

01:07.115 --> 01:08.742
You maybe wanna go together?

01:08.825 --> 01:11.495
My friend's performing in it,
so I wanna go support.

01:11.995 --> 01:13.997
But I'm too chicken to go by myself.

01:16.166 --> 01:17.793
Sure. Let's do it.

01:18.752 --> 01:21.463
I'll ask around,
see if anyone else wants to come too.

01:22.130 --> 01:22.964
Hm…

01:24.132 --> 01:26.051
The bigger audience the better, right?

01:26.718 --> 01:28.136
Yeah, I guess you're right.

01:28.804 --> 01:30.097
Ah. I'm sorry.

01:30.180 --> 01:31.431
I didn't mean to bother you.

01:31.515 --> 01:34.976
I just figured it was easier and faster
to call than type it all out in a text,

01:35.060 --> 01:35.894
y'know?

01:36.978 --> 01:38.396
Easier and faster, huh?

01:38.939 --> 01:39.773
Well,

01:39.856 --> 01:42.067
I'll reach out
again closer to the concert.

01:42.150 --> 01:44.361
Cool. Sounds good.

01:45.987 --> 01:46.822
Hm.

01:46.905 --> 01:48.657
LIFT
SIDE PLANK

01:55.789 --> 01:58.125
The rain… It just won't stop.

01:59.626 --> 02:02.045
MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

02:05.048 --> 02:05.924
I like you.

02:08.218 --> 02:10.971
Today, when I run into Yota in class

02:11.596 --> 02:13.014
how should I approach him?

02:13.682 --> 02:16.059
Would it hurt him
to act like nothing happened?

02:16.726 --> 02:18.895
Avoiding him would hurt more,
wouldn't it?

02:19.688 --> 02:20.522
Wait.

02:20.605 --> 02:23.650
Aren't I hurting him more by not
being able to return his feelings

02:23.733 --> 02:24.693
in the first place?

02:25.735 --> 02:26.611
What should I do?

02:28.572 --> 02:29.406
Miki.

02:31.616 --> 02:32.450
Morning.

02:34.202 --> 02:35.370
You ready for the quiz?

02:35.453 --> 02:37.205
The one for Japanese class?

02:38.874 --> 02:40.458
Huh?! That was today?!

02:40.542 --> 02:41.459
Crap!

02:42.961 --> 02:44.963
There's still time. Don't worry.

02:45.046 --> 02:46.965
You just need to memorize the handout.

02:47.048 --> 02:48.258
Oh, there you go again!

02:48.341 --> 02:51.887
"You just have to memorize it!"
Like it's the easiest thing in the world.

02:51.970 --> 02:52.929
Seriously…

02:54.097 --> 02:55.015
Hey, don't stress.

02:55.098 --> 02:56.016
You've got this.

02:56.600 --> 02:59.060
Hey, Yota! We're goin' on ahead.

02:59.644 --> 03:00.478
Oh, wait up.

03:02.230 --> 03:03.773
Well, See you later.

03:18.205 --> 03:20.040
Why's he gotta be so nice?

03:27.756 --> 03:28.715
BANANA DRINK
GENTLE SWEETNESS OF RIPE BANANA

03:28.798 --> 03:31.134
So, Miki. Something happened, right?

03:32.510 --> 03:33.762
No, nothing happened.

03:34.346 --> 03:35.180
Here, try this.

03:38.058 --> 03:39.017
SIP

03:42.312 --> 03:43.480
Tell me, Minato.

03:44.272 --> 03:45.106
Hm?

03:45.190 --> 03:48.360
You casually date chicks you're not
into all the time, right?

03:48.443 --> 03:49.819
Woah. Random.

03:49.903 --> 03:50.737
And kinda rude.

03:51.446 --> 03:52.572
Ever turn someone down

03:53.240 --> 03:55.075
after they confessed their feelings?

03:57.035 --> 03:58.036
Uh…

03:58.578 --> 04:00.872
- I guess not.
- Why not?

04:01.706 --> 04:03.833
It's not that I had
a reason to date them.

04:04.334 --> 04:06.294
But I guess I also didn't have a reason…

04:06.378 --> 04:07.462
Not to date them.

04:09.256 --> 04:10.257
Okay, but afterward

04:10.757 --> 04:13.260
do you ever regret deciding to date them?

04:14.594 --> 04:16.012
Since I'm usually the dumpee

04:16.763 --> 04:18.682
they clearly regret dating me.

04:19.224 --> 04:20.517
Hence, the dumping.

04:21.434 --> 04:24.562
If they said they didn't want to be
with me, then that was that.

04:24.646 --> 04:26.898
There was no point
in fighting it or begging.

04:28.316 --> 04:29.234
I wonder…

04:30.151 --> 04:33.905
if it was painful for them knowing
you had different feelings than they do.

04:35.824 --> 04:37.409
UH, WHAT?
AM I BEING ATTACKED?

04:37.492 --> 04:38.785
GUILT

04:40.745 --> 04:43.331
Someday, when you finally
fall in love with someone

04:43.915 --> 04:45.709
and they don't care about you at all,

04:45.792 --> 04:48.628
I hope it really pushes you
over the deep end, man.

04:50.672 --> 04:52.340
Yeah. Possibly.

04:53.466 --> 04:55.552
The pain of unrequited feelings…

04:56.386 --> 04:57.387
I get it now.

04:58.471 --> 05:00.056
I never thought of it that way.

05:00.932 --> 05:02.600
I feel like I've been a jerk

05:02.684 --> 05:04.227
to all the girls I've dated.

05:05.103 --> 05:07.147
So then that's how it goes,

05:07.772 --> 05:08.898
it never works out.

05:09.691 --> 05:10.984
Yeah- Wait, hold up.

05:11.484 --> 05:12.569
Wait. Uh-

05:12.652 --> 05:15.905
Are you trying to tell me somone
confessed their feelings to you

05:15.989 --> 05:18.992
and you're debating whether
you should turn them down?

05:20.702 --> 05:21.536
Oh crap.

05:22.037 --> 05:23.997
I just said the wrong thing, didn't I?

05:24.080 --> 05:25.206
No, I…

05:26.583 --> 05:27.417
Already did.

05:31.546 --> 05:32.380
Huh?

05:33.965 --> 05:36.426
That's what happened. Guess it's over.

05:38.720 --> 05:39.554
Well hey,

05:39.637 --> 05:41.931
since I knew nothing
would come of it anyway…

05:42.849 --> 05:46.227
I'm glad I got it out
and don't have to keep it bottled up.

05:47.520 --> 05:49.564
You are? Really?

05:50.065 --> 05:50.899
Yep.

05:52.650 --> 05:53.485
But,

05:53.985 --> 05:56.863
I'm also bummed thinking
like "Aw, it's over."

05:57.530 --> 06:00.950
Now it feels like there's
this giant empty space inside me,

06:01.034 --> 06:02.619
that that feeling used to fill.

06:04.496 --> 06:05.789
How should I put it?

06:06.623 --> 06:09.417
Now I just want… to fill that void.

06:10.210 --> 06:11.086
Yota

06:11.586 --> 06:13.338
Is he crying…? You can cry.

06:14.172 --> 06:15.799
- Huh?
- Uh…

06:16.299 --> 06:17.675
He's not crying…

06:18.676 --> 06:19.511
Oh, um…

06:19.594 --> 06:22.347
I-I thought you might need
something to cry into.

06:23.640 --> 06:25.266
Thanks, but I'm okay.

06:25.767 --> 06:28.269
Is this something people
usually cry over?

06:28.978 --> 06:30.855
I wouldn't know, I can't cry.

06:31.856 --> 06:35.527
Don't get me wrong, I feel sad at times.
Graduation ceremonies…

06:35.610 --> 06:37.737
or after losing a big game, but…

06:37.821 --> 06:38.696
at some point

06:39.197 --> 06:42.951
I gave up on getting worked up over
things because that's just how life is.

06:43.785 --> 06:47.038
When my emotions get too big
I let them escape through tears.

06:48.081 --> 06:50.250
But,
Yota keeps them all bottled up inside.

06:51.584 --> 06:53.128
I mean, I like this guy,

06:53.211 --> 06:54.129
but if I'm honest,

06:54.629 --> 06:56.589
I've only ever liked him as a friend.

06:57.882 --> 07:00.176
And not as a boyfriend or anything.

07:02.554 --> 07:03.555
Back in junior high

07:04.055 --> 07:06.474
I guess I dated a few guys
here and there but,

07:07.475 --> 07:11.104
Whenever they would give me their number,
I would feel this… I don't know…

07:11.187 --> 07:13.022
a feeling I could never quite place.

07:13.940 --> 07:16.818
They'd give off vibes of
"someone I could end up dating."

07:16.901 --> 07:17.902
I FEEL LIKE HE MIGHT BE A GOOD GUY

07:17.986 --> 07:19.529
I felt butterflies in my stomach

07:19.612 --> 07:22.449
and dated them thinking I
might like them back, but…

07:22.949 --> 07:25.326
I GOT DUMPED AGAIN!

07:25.410 --> 07:27.745
It never worked out in the end,
and every time…

07:27.829 --> 07:29.497
I felt like I was being rejected.

07:29.581 --> 07:30.999
FINE, WHATEVER I'LL FORGET ABOUT IT…

07:32.125 --> 07:34.752
I wasn't really seeing
them for who they were either.

07:34.836 --> 07:35.670
- So…
- Hmph…

07:35.753 --> 07:39.174
I've never- Never had a real relationship.

07:40.800 --> 07:43.553
I was just happy that
someone liked me, y'know?

07:43.636 --> 07:47.640
So if I date this guy despite not
feeling the same way yet… that's like…

07:48.141 --> 07:50.852
I'd be leading him on
just to not hurt his feelings.

07:52.103 --> 07:53.813
And I- I just know

07:54.314 --> 07:56.441
I'll end up hating myself in the end.

07:57.817 --> 07:58.651
So

07:59.319 --> 08:01.279
I don't think I'm in the wrong here.

08:02.572 --> 08:03.740
But I feel…

08:04.574 --> 08:05.992
So miserable.

08:11.414 --> 08:12.248
Miki,

08:12.332 --> 08:16.127
would you rather have had Yota
just keep treating you as a friend?

08:18.671 --> 08:20.715
Huh? What?! Why'd you-

08:20.798 --> 08:21.925
It's Yota, isn't it?

08:22.425 --> 08:23.885
I can tell just by looking.

08:24.719 --> 08:26.804
Oh… So that means…

08:27.722 --> 08:30.225
I was the only one who didn't notice it.

08:30.975 --> 08:32.602
Throwing things around like

08:32.685 --> 08:34.354
"friend," and… "I love you"…

08:34.854 --> 08:35.855
I'm such a-

08:37.148 --> 08:38.566
An insensitive jerk.

08:39.734 --> 08:41.027
Why am I so awful?

08:46.074 --> 08:46.950
What should I do?

08:48.201 --> 08:49.536
I'm miserable.

08:51.412 --> 08:53.498
Look, you can't blame yourself, Miki.

08:54.374 --> 08:55.708
It's not his fault either.

08:56.251 --> 08:59.629
I'd think that if you found out that
someone you thought of as just a friend

08:59.712 --> 09:02.298
actually liked you in a
different way than you did…

09:02.840 --> 09:05.426
And once you realized they
look at you in that way…

09:05.927 --> 09:08.179
It would feel a bit disgusting,
wouldn't it?

09:08.263 --> 09:09.180
CRACK

09:09.681 --> 09:11.140
I find people tend to fall

09:11.641 --> 09:13.726
without even realizing it's happening.

09:14.561 --> 09:17.897
Once they're in love, even if the
other person doesn't feel the same…

09:17.981 --> 09:18.898
And also…

09:19.399 --> 09:20.441
Madam Koyun said

09:20.525 --> 09:25.196
the people she considers friends would
never become potential love interests.

09:27.699 --> 09:30.368
They're mentally prepared to
get hurt to some extent.

09:31.953 --> 09:32.912
Seriously…

09:33.621 --> 09:35.456
Who am I trying to convince here?

09:36.916 --> 09:37.792
I…

09:39.210 --> 09:40.878
These feelings I have…

09:44.799 --> 09:45.633
I'm so hungry.

09:46.134 --> 09:46.968
- Oh, hey there!
- Huh?

09:47.051 --> 09:47.885
- Huh?
- Huh?

09:48.511 --> 09:51.180
PEOPLE WHO STARTED MINGLING
AT SOME POINT IN THE CHEER SQUAD

09:51.264 --> 09:52.140
This concert

09:52.223 --> 09:54.058
is shaping up to be really fun!

09:54.142 --> 09:55.268
Oh, You're coming too?

09:55.768 --> 09:56.853
Yep!

09:56.936 --> 09:58.187
I'm going with Amamiya.

09:58.771 --> 10:00.023
OH, REALLY…?

10:00.523 --> 10:01.566
Huh?

10:01.649 --> 10:02.734
Are you two… a thing?

10:03.234 --> 10:04.277
Oh, no, we're not.

10:04.777 --> 10:07.822
We're planning to invite more
people so it's a group thing.

10:07.905 --> 10:10.074
I'm pretty sure it's
his way of dodging me

10:10.158 --> 10:11.492
cause I'm being pushy.

10:12.035 --> 10:13.995
- Huh?
- See you later.

10:17.040 --> 10:18.541
Is he dodging her or is it…

10:18.625 --> 10:19.542
In her head?

10:20.043 --> 10:21.002
Who knows, man?

10:21.502 --> 10:24.172
Either way,
I'm worried she's gonna end up in tears.

10:26.716 --> 10:28.384
GRADE 2 CLASS 2

10:28.968 --> 10:29.802
Miki…

10:30.428 --> 10:31.846
Do you have work today?

10:31.929 --> 10:33.514
Hm? I don't.

10:34.182 --> 10:35.892
Do you… Wanna hang out then?

10:36.392 --> 10:37.644
Uh Sure.

10:38.645 --> 10:40.730
She's the one… inviting me out?

10:41.648 --> 10:44.275
There are so many things I
want to ask Miki about

10:44.859 --> 10:47.737
But then… there's also
so much I haven't told her yet.

10:48.655 --> 10:50.198
Especially about Amamiya.

10:50.740 --> 10:52.325
But after hiding it for so long

10:53.159 --> 10:55.620
it feels embarrassing to
suddenly bring it up now.

10:55.703 --> 10:57.914
It's gonna come completely
out of left field.

10:57.997 --> 11:00.541
With all these thoughts
jumbled up in my head…

11:00.625 --> 11:03.753
I'm worried I'll trip over my
words and it'll come out all wrong.

11:03.836 --> 11:04.962
Oh no, is this…

11:05.046 --> 11:06.381
a serious conversation?

11:06.881 --> 11:08.758
A consultation? What do I do?

11:08.841 --> 11:11.260
The truth is… My feelings for Yota…

11:11.344 --> 11:12.387
Is that what it is?!

11:12.470 --> 11:14.931
What should I say, and how
much should I spill?

11:17.308 --> 11:18.142
Yota?

11:18.810 --> 11:21.104
You wanna… maybe grab some food?

11:24.899 --> 11:27.610
Mm hm. Sounds good, I'm all yours buddy.

11:28.444 --> 11:31.531
Oh… well… I didn't exactly
mean like for a venting session.

11:34.992 --> 11:37.245
Ooh. These are the tastiest ones!

11:38.246 --> 11:39.205
- Miki.
- Huh?

11:39.288 --> 11:41.457
- Well, um…
- What did you get?

11:41.541 --> 11:44.127
There's uh…
Something I wanna to talk to you about.

11:46.045 --> 11:47.255
It's uh… About…

11:47.755 --> 11:49.757
- Amamiy-
- Man, it's been forever.

11:50.508 --> 11:53.720
C'mon Yota. Whenever I invite you out
you always turn me down.

11:53.803 --> 11:55.847
Ah please, that's not true.

11:57.098 --> 11:58.516
I think that might be-

11:58.599 --> 11:59.517
No,

11:59.600 --> 12:01.894
- it's definitely them.
- Really?

12:01.978 --> 12:03.354
Fine, whatever, then.

12:04.063 --> 12:04.939
- Yota!
- Amamiya!

12:05.565 --> 12:07.442
So uh… Minato…

12:08.025 --> 12:11.154
- Huh?
- Are you gonna go out with Kurita?

12:16.159 --> 12:17.160
So, Minato

12:17.785 --> 12:18.619
Hm?

12:19.203 --> 12:20.997
Are you gonna go out with Kurita?

12:22.206 --> 12:23.040
With Kurita?

12:24.125 --> 12:25.042
- Who?
- Who?

12:25.585 --> 12:26.836
You mean Kuriki?

12:27.628 --> 12:29.130
Huh? Uh,

12:29.213 --> 12:30.673
Yeah, the first-year student.

12:31.758 --> 12:33.551
Wait, why are you bringing her up?

12:34.135 --> 12:36.971
You're going to the concert,
right? Just the two of you?

12:37.054 --> 12:38.848
Eh, it's just a concert though.

12:39.348 --> 12:41.684
Besides,
I was thinking of inviting more people.

12:41.768 --> 12:42.977
So, you should come too.

12:43.686 --> 12:45.605
Minato, hear me out.

12:46.105 --> 12:49.525
Ever since junior high, you've always
gotten too flirty with girls,

12:49.609 --> 12:51.903
which gets their hopes up
and leads them on.

12:51.986 --> 12:52.987
Should we-

12:53.070 --> 12:54.906
really be eavesdropping like this?

12:54.989 --> 12:56.949
Well, it's too late to leave now.

12:57.742 --> 13:01.162
You've had a zillion failed
relationships because of it.

13:01.913 --> 13:02.747
Huh?

13:03.623 --> 13:04.457
Here I was,

13:04.540 --> 13:08.085
thinking that Yota had finally
come to confide in me about his problems.

13:08.169 --> 13:11.047
But instead he's ripping me
a new one just like Miki did.

13:12.089 --> 13:13.549
Wait so… you're saying…

13:13.633 --> 13:17.929
I should start rejecting anyone I don't
necessarily have romantic feelings for?

13:18.679 --> 13:20.014
If I don't hate that person,

13:20.097 --> 13:22.767
don't you think I should at least
give them a chance?

13:22.850 --> 13:24.769
I'm not saying you should go that far…

13:24.852 --> 13:25.686
But,

13:26.187 --> 13:28.815
just stop giving girls the wrong idea,
okay?

13:29.607 --> 13:30.441
Is that cause-

13:31.275 --> 13:33.194
you didn't like when it happened to you?

13:33.277 --> 13:34.946
This has nothing to do with Miki!

13:37.990 --> 13:38.825
I…

13:41.035 --> 13:43.538
- Sorry.
- No, I'm sorry too…

13:44.080 --> 13:45.456
I went too far.

13:46.541 --> 13:47.458
Yota…

13:47.542 --> 13:48.459
TEARS WELLING UP

13:48.960 --> 13:51.504
Oh gosh…
I haven't even told Koyun anything yet…

13:52.004 --> 13:54.757
Hang on, Minato. How much do you know?

13:55.258 --> 13:57.051
Pretty much everything. Sorry.

13:59.512 --> 14:02.014
I'm sorry for putting you
in such a weird position.

14:02.098 --> 14:03.307
That's okay, no worries.

14:04.350 --> 14:05.393
So, Minato…

14:05.893 --> 14:08.688
- Huh?
- Have you ever fallen in love?

14:10.565 --> 14:11.482
Fallen in love?

14:12.024 --> 14:14.610
Yeah, like,
"no one can replace this person," or

14:14.694 --> 14:16.904
"They're the only one for me,"
or something.

14:18.030 --> 14:18.865
Honestly,

14:19.407 --> 14:21.242
I feel that way about everyone!

14:23.494 --> 14:25.121
Even about you and Miki.

14:25.705 --> 14:27.957
You're both irreplaceable friends to me.

14:29.041 --> 14:29.917
What about Koyun?

14:32.712 --> 14:34.881
Koyun… Is great, isn't she?

14:35.715 --> 14:37.258
The four of us have a great time together

14:37.341 --> 14:38.676
and you two get along really well,

14:39.969 --> 14:42.013
don't you? Do you think there might be…

14:42.096 --> 14:43.097
something there?

14:44.432 --> 14:45.892
Yeah. Koyun is very…

14:47.935 --> 14:48.769
I like her.

14:50.479 --> 14:51.606
As a friend, you know.

14:53.065 --> 14:54.525
I really like her a lot.

14:57.445 --> 14:58.279
Oh.

14:59.322 --> 15:00.865
Well man, I hope one day

15:00.948 --> 15:02.742
you feel that way about someone.

15:05.202 --> 15:06.329
Hey, who knows.

15:07.413 --> 15:09.415
I hope I can show you that side someday.

15:13.628 --> 15:16.547
- Oh…
- I hate rainy season. It's so humid.

15:18.257 --> 15:19.091
Koyun…

15:21.427 --> 15:23.137
Miki, sorry…

15:23.679 --> 15:24.513
But I-

15:25.056 --> 15:26.182
Fell in love with him.

15:27.600 --> 15:29.352
You- Yota-

15:29.435 --> 15:30.478
I fell for Amamiya.

15:33.230 --> 15:36.275
Wait, what?
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

15:36.359 --> 15:38.069
Sorry I couldn't tell you.

15:39.153 --> 15:41.113
I wasn't sure of my feelings yet.

15:42.031 --> 15:44.742
And I didn't know what I even wanted so

15:44.825 --> 15:45.993
I never told you.

15:46.494 --> 15:48.204
Okay, wait… I can't…

15:48.287 --> 15:49.205
Really? So…

15:49.747 --> 15:50.957
This whole time, I was…

15:51.582 --> 15:54.085
Don't try to put the
moves on her or be weird!

15:54.168 --> 15:56.921
Yeah. This is a great idea!

15:57.713 --> 16:01.175
Crap… This sucks… This is…
the crappiest crap that ever crapped.

16:02.551 --> 16:03.469
I'm gonna barf.

16:03.970 --> 16:04.804
Argh-

16:06.097 --> 16:07.348
Um… Miki…

16:08.015 --> 16:10.768
I promise you
I knew nothing was gonna come from it.

16:11.268 --> 16:14.605
Plus, he just clearly said that
we're only friends, so don't worry.

16:14.689 --> 16:16.232
Huh? No, wait.

16:16.315 --> 16:17.316
I was referring to-

16:17.400 --> 16:18.693
How I feel about myself.

16:19.193 --> 16:20.236
Huh?

16:20.319 --> 16:21.821
The whole time, I thought-

16:21.904 --> 16:23.531
This was what was going.

16:25.199 --> 16:26.492
And I thought-

16:27.284 --> 16:29.370
Huh? B-B-But- back then, and I- and that-

16:29.453 --> 16:31.914
- and this… And then you- but he was-
- Huh? But you seemed so- Oh,

16:31.998 --> 16:33.082
I misread everything-

16:34.208 --> 16:35.960
ALL MISUNDERSTANDINGS WERE CLEARED UP

16:36.043 --> 16:38.129
So, does that mean this whole time

16:38.629 --> 16:40.673
I've been screwing up Yota's love life?

16:40.756 --> 16:41.799
No! That's not it!

16:42.717 --> 16:43.551
Ultimately,

16:43.634 --> 16:46.220
I always thought of Yota
and I as just friends.

16:47.138 --> 16:49.265
Miki… previously,

16:49.348 --> 16:51.642
you talked about maybe
being open to romance

16:52.143 --> 16:53.602
and getting a boyfriend.

16:53.686 --> 16:54.645
But you…

16:55.146 --> 16:56.564
don't want that to be him?

16:58.607 --> 16:59.442
Let's just say,

17:00.067 --> 17:01.027
hypothetically,

17:01.527 --> 17:05.114
if I confessed to you out of the blue
that I always liked you romantically,

17:05.197 --> 17:07.158
do you think
you could just switch gears and say,

17:07.241 --> 17:09.994
"Sure, I've never though of
you that way, but why not?"

17:10.077 --> 17:11.078
Good point.

17:11.996 --> 17:15.082
I just… knew I couldn't do that so easily.

17:15.750 --> 17:16.584
Someone

17:16.667 --> 17:20.254
confessing their love to me makes me
feel worse than I thought it would.

17:20.337 --> 17:21.338
But… there's also a selfish part of me

17:21.422 --> 17:24.383
that thinks it would be easier if
I could just learn to love someone

17:24.467 --> 17:25.801
who loves me already.

17:25.885 --> 17:28.137
I turned him down because I
thought I would hurt him

17:28.220 --> 17:30.181
if my heart wasn't really in it.

17:30.723 --> 17:32.975
But then I ended up hurting him anyway.

17:33.809 --> 17:36.395
So then what should I have said to him?

17:38.147 --> 17:39.690
Miki. Listen,

17:40.232 --> 17:42.276
The way Yota feels towards you,

17:43.861 --> 17:44.904
Isn't sexual.

17:45.529 --> 17:46.906
SEXUAL DESIRE

17:46.989 --> 17:50.743
His interactions with you were never
fueled by desire to date you or touch

17:50.826 --> 17:53.871
- you, or hold you or anything physical.
- What are you saying?

17:53.954 --> 17:56.832
He likes you for you.
He likes you as a friend too.

17:57.875 --> 17:59.168
He genuinely sees you

17:59.794 --> 18:01.295
and likes you for who you are.

18:02.004 --> 18:02.922
This whole time,

18:03.464 --> 18:06.634
the only thing on Yota's mind
has been how to make you happy.

18:07.676 --> 18:10.429
He isn't thinking about
having "you" make "him" happy.

18:11.055 --> 18:12.139
That's not who he is.

18:13.015 --> 18:13.849
So then,

18:15.017 --> 18:18.145
don't blame yourself for
anything that happens with Yota.

18:20.022 --> 18:20.981
To me, you're Miki.

18:21.607 --> 18:23.275
You're not just some girl.

18:28.823 --> 18:30.908
Today… I…

18:31.867 --> 18:34.328
When Yota came over
near where I was sitting

18:35.162 --> 18:36.664
I- I looked away.

18:38.999 --> 18:39.917
Starting tomorrow…

18:40.417 --> 18:41.627
I'll be more-

18:43.003 --> 18:43.838
Yeah.

18:48.634 --> 18:50.803
CLICKETY CLACKETY
CLICKETY CLACKETY

18:50.886 --> 18:53.430
PUFFY EYES

18:53.514 --> 18:54.890
What's your plan? So

18:54.974 --> 18:56.225
Huh? Plan for what?

18:56.725 --> 18:57.685
Minato.

18:57.768 --> 18:59.103
Will you tell him how you feel?

18:59.186 --> 19:00.938
No, no, no, n-no! Never! No way.

19:01.021 --> 19:02.022
Oh-

19:02.523 --> 19:03.941
Since I've known you,

19:04.024 --> 19:07.653
This is the first time you've opened up
to me about something like this.

19:07.736 --> 19:09.697
I wanna have your back and support you.

19:10.906 --> 19:11.740
Well thank you.

19:12.241 --> 19:13.075
Although

19:13.159 --> 19:15.661
after finding out he only
sees me as a friend,

19:15.744 --> 19:18.747
I think I want to shut my
feeling sdown while I still can.

19:18.831 --> 19:20.541
I mean if you think about it

19:20.624 --> 19:22.793
isn't it be better
to keep him as a friend?

19:23.377 --> 19:26.422
Plus, I don't think someone like me
with no experience would be able to

19:26.505 --> 19:27.506
win him over anyway.

19:28.924 --> 19:30.593
HARD TO DENY

19:32.261 --> 19:34.346
Let's all just hang out as friends again.

19:36.015 --> 19:36.849
Yeah.

19:42.021 --> 19:43.439
If I don't hate that person…

19:43.522 --> 19:46.233
don't you think I should at
least give them a chance?

19:46.984 --> 19:49.486
The kindness and affection
Minato gave so readily,

19:49.570 --> 19:52.406
were the same he gave… to everyone.

19:53.157 --> 19:55.326
I thought I was special and read into it.

19:55.409 --> 19:56.952
I got carried away.

19:57.620 --> 19:58.454
I'm just-

19:59.955 --> 20:02.499
How… How could I be so stupid?

20:19.892 --> 20:20.726
It's okay.

20:27.191 --> 20:28.025
I'll…

20:29.276 --> 20:30.110
I'll be alright.

20:33.155 --> 20:34.114
Time to move on.

20:35.366 --> 20:38.535
At the start, I didn't even
remotely want to date him anyway.

20:39.578 --> 20:40.412
That's why

20:40.955 --> 20:43.540
I was so distant when we first met.
And yet-

20:44.458 --> 20:45.584
As a friend, you know.

20:46.460 --> 20:47.670
I really like her a lot.

20:48.754 --> 20:51.298
At the end of the day,
just hearing him say that

20:51.382 --> 20:52.841
is more than enough for me.

20:53.676 --> 20:54.510
And really,

20:54.593 --> 20:58.555
maybe I should be questioning the nature
of my feelings in the first place.

20:59.390 --> 21:03.227
I used to always be the one to
reject everyone around me so maybe

21:04.603 --> 21:06.522
I was just feeling lonely.

21:08.107 --> 21:10.484
If that's all it was then I'm okay.

21:11.485 --> 21:13.112
If I'm happy how things are now

21:13.195 --> 21:14.571
I won't feel lonely.

21:16.323 --> 21:17.783
And it's not too late

21:19.076 --> 21:20.494
to start back at square one.

21:22.496 --> 21:23.330
Morning.

21:24.039 --> 21:24.873
Uh-

21:25.499 --> 21:26.333
Good morning.

21:26.417 --> 21:28.002
GRADE 2 CLASS 2

21:28.085 --> 21:28.919
Huh?

21:29.837 --> 21:30.796
You're early today.

21:31.922 --> 21:33.257
Good morning, Minato!

21:33.340 --> 21:34.300
Woah, alright.

21:35.175 --> 21:36.093
Morning to you too!

21:36.176 --> 21:37.469
Oh. Good- good morning.

21:39.054 --> 21:39.888
Hm?

21:41.515 --> 21:42.599
Good morning, Yota!

21:47.771 --> 21:49.064
I like the energy.

21:49.148 --> 21:50.065
Morning.

23:39.341 --> 23:40.509
If things stay this way

23:41.260 --> 23:42.261
then my feelings…

23:43.762 --> 23:46.306
are nothing more than a bad joke.

23:47.975 --> 23:52.062
I mean, the thought of her maybe
seeing me the same way one day…

23:53.230 --> 23:54.648
Is that even possible?
